Package: ollama
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, libvulkan1
Suggests: ollama-cuda, ollama-rocm
Description: run language models on this computer (Ollama)
 Ollama answers programs on this computer that ask a language model for
 text: KMail and the other KDE programs through KDE's text add-ons, Vibe,
 and mail add-ons. It runs models on the processor, and on the graphics card
 through Vulkan (AMD, Intel and NVIDIA).
 .
 This is upstream's own build of Ollama 0.40.16 (MIT,
 https://github.com/ollama/ollama), repackaged. The release has no
 signature for its Linux bundles: the bundle was checked by its size and
 SHA-256 against the release's own checksum list, which comes from the same
 origin as the file. The source package carries the tagged source and the
 release files it installs.
 .
 Nothing runs after installation: the user service ollama.service is not
 enabled. No model is in the package; models are downloaded only when the
 person asks for one. Models hosted by Ollama's own service (their names end
 in ":cloud") send what the person writes to that service.

Package: ollama-cuda
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ollama (= ${binary:Version}),
 cuda-cudart-13-5 | cuda-cudart-13-4 | cuda-cudart-13-3 | cuda-cudart-13-2 | cuda-cudart-13-1,
 libcublas-13-5 | libcublas-13-4 | libcublas-13-3 | libcublas-13-2 | libcublas-13-1,
 cuda-nvrtc-13-5 | cuda-nvrtc-13-4 | cuda-nvrtc-13-3 | cuda-nvrtc-13-2 | cuda-nvrtc-13-1,
 libnvjitlink-13-5 | libnvjitlink-13-4 | libnvjitlink-13-3 | libnvjitlink-13-2 | libnvjitlink-13-1,
 libnvfatbin-13-5 | libnvfatbin-13-4 | libnvfatbin-13-3 | libnvfatbin-13-2 | libnvfatbin-13-1,
 libcuda1
Enhances: ollama
Description: run Ollama's models on NVIDIA cards with CUDA 13
 Ollama's runner for NVIDIA graphics cards through CUDA 13 (Turing and
 newer), 281 MB: upstream's build of llama.cpp's CUDA back end.
 .
 NVIDIA's CUDA libraries are not in this package: NVIDIA's licence lets an
 application's developer distribute them. They come from NVIDIA's own
 repository, which the edition's hardware setup configures on a computer
 with an NVIDIA card. Cards that only run CUDA 12 (Maxwell, Pascal, Volta)
 use the Vulkan runner of the ollama package.

Package: ollama-rocm
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ollama (= ${binary:Version})
Enhances: ollama
Description: run Ollama's models on AMD cards with ROCm 7.2
 Ollama's runner for AMD graphics cards through ROCm 7.2, 2.7 GB:
 upstream's build of llama.cpp's HIP back end with AMD's ROCm 7.2.1
 libraries (HIP, rocBLAS, rocSOLVER, hipBLAS, hipBLASLt and their runtime).
 Debian ships ROCm 6.4, which this runner cannot load, so AMD's libraries
 come with it; Debian's libdrm, libnuma and libelf serve it.
 Every AMD card also runs models through the Vulkan runner of the ollama
 package.
